<section class="section section-top-tight">
  <div class="container">
    <span class="eyebrow">Overview</span>
    <h2>Introduction</h2>
    <p class="prose">
      Starrydata2 is a web system that extracts experimental data from figures in published papers on inorganic materials (primarily thermoelectric, magnetic, and other physical properties), converts them into structured curves, and stores them alongside sample information such as composition and fabrication process. As of 2026, the database contains more than <strong><span data-counts="curves">194,000</span>&nbsp;curves</strong>, <strong><span data-counts="samples">82,000</span>&nbsp;samples</strong>, and <strong><span data-counts="papers">13,000</span>&nbsp;papers</strong>
      (see the homepage statistics for the latest numbers).
    </p>
    <p class="prose">
      All data are available <strong>free of charge for both commercial and non-commercial use</strong>,
      and can be downloaded as CSV or JSON files from the web.
      Any registered researcher can participate in data registration (curation).
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

